          <Pad Id="KZmc1txyRDlLqxlK1qqvQr" Comment="Active" Bounds="1531,420,35,35" ShowValueBox="true" isIOBox="true" />
          <Pad Id="UR4WMyoqQdQNBs4tjNfbgA" Comment="Active Color" Bounds="1651,470,136,15" ShowValueBox="true" isIOBox="true" />
          <Pad Id="V6dSWkPWtJjNEv29A0gegm" Comment="Fade Gain" Bounds="1631,420,35,15" ShowValueBox="true" isIOBox="true" />
          <Pad Id="Cw6ZKh1N0PJOh1j6xlUaWG" Bounds="-194,-215,635,1238" ShowValueBox="true" isIOBox="true" Value="============================================================&#xD;&#xA; VL.Interpole — timeline / sequencer node&#xD;&#xA;============================================================&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;WHAT IT IS&#xD;&#xA;  A multi-track timeline editor (clips, keyframes, markers, loop&#xD;&#xA;  region, audio) rendered as a VL.Skia layer. It edits in-patch and&#xD;&#xA;  drives downstream nodes from the playhead.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;WIRING (minimum)&#xD;&#xA;  Interpole.Editor  -&gt; Renderer (Skia)      // shows the editor&#xD;&#xA;  Interpole.Audio   -&gt; VL.Audio out         // only if you use audio tracks&#xD;&#xA;  Interpole.Info    -&gt; Get… splitters        // read the timeline state&#xD;&#xA;  Leave Data unconnected — the node stores the timeline on it and&#xD;&#xA;  saves it with the patch.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;EDITOR — MOUSE&#xD;&#xA;  Double-click empty lane ....... add a clip (audio track = file picker)&#xD;&#xA;  Drag clip ..................... move (also between tracks)&#xD;&#xA;  Drag clip left/right edge ..... resize / trim&#xD;&#xA;  Drag clip top corners ......... fade in / out&#xD;&#xA;  Double-click clip label ....... rename + colour&#xD;&#xA;  Double-click clip body ........ open its keyframe page&#xD;&#xA;  Drag on empty lane ............ marquee select&#xD;&#xA;  Right-click a keyframe ........ easing menu&#xD;&#xA;  Right-drag ............... pan      Mouse wheel ... zoom&#xD;&#xA;  Ruler top strip .......... drag the loop region&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;EDITOR — DELETE&#xD;&#xA;  Del ........................... delete selected clips (timeline)&#xD;&#xA;                                  or keyframes (clip page)&#xD;&#xA;  Alt/Middle-click clip ......... delete that clip&#xD;&#xA;  Alt/Middle-click track header . delete the track AND its clips&#xD;&#xA;  Alt/Middle-click keyframe ..... delete that keyframe&#xD;&#xA;  Alt/Middle-click marker ....... delete that marker&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;EDITOR — KEYS&#xD;&#xA;  Space play/stop   Ctrl+C/V copy/paste   Ctrl+Z/Y undo/redo&#xD;&#xA;  B / N = set loop in / out to the playhead&#xD;&#xA;  Padlock = lock all editing (playback stays live)&#xD;&#xA;  Stopwatch = toggle frames / timecode display&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;TRANSPORT PINS (rising-edge bangs unless noted)&#xD;&#xA;  Play / Stop / Rewind .... start / halt+save / go to 0&#xD;&#xA;  Loop .................... on-off state (two-way, agrees with the button)&#xD;&#xA;  Loop In / Loop Out ...... loop region in frames (0,0 = whole content)&#xD;&#xA;  Time + Set .............. jump the playhead to Time when Set fires&#xD;&#xA;  Marker + Jump ........... jump to a named marker&#xD;&#xA;  Active State ............ string; matching a marker name seeks+plays&#xD;&#xA;                            (wire VL.Automata GetActiveState here)&#xD;&#xA;  Fps ..................... playback rate + timecode (default 60)&#xD;&#xA;  No UI Mode .............. headless: skip drawing, keep playing + outputs&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;OUTPUTS&#xD;&#xA;  Current Frame, Is Playing, Active Marker, plus per-track spreads:&#xD;&#xA;  Active Clip Name / Clip Frame / Clip Length / Clip Progress /&#xD;&#xA;  Fade Gain / Active Color / Upcoming Clip Names / Track Names.&#xD;&#xA;  Track Levels = per audio-track VU.  Info bundles it all on one pin.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;READING STATE (splitters off Info)&#xD;&#xA;  GetTransport ...... current frame, is playing, active marker&#xD;&#xA;  GetTrack &lt;name&gt; ... the active clip's values on one track&#xD;&#xA;  GetClip &lt;name&gt; .... one clip by name: Active + its clip values&#xD;&#xA;  GetKeyframes &lt;clip&gt; float-track names + current values&#xD;&#xA;  GetActiveClips / GetUpcomingClips / GetActiveMarker&#xD;&#xA;============================================================">
            <p:TypeAnnotation LastCategoryFullName="Primitive" LastDependency="VL.CoreLib.vl">
              <Choice Kind="TypeFlag" Name="String" />
            </p:TypeAnnotation>
            <p:ValueBoxSettings>
              <p:fontsize p:Type="Int32">9</p:fontsize>
              <p:stringtype p:Assembly="VL.Core" p:Type="VL.Core.StringType">Comment</p:stringtype>
            </p:ValueBoxSettings>
          </Pad>
        </Canvas>
